    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Based on this experiment, how many marbles of each colour do you think there are? Justify your answer mathematically.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately 2 red, 3 green and 5 blue marbles.",
          "worked": "Using relative frequencies, the estimated numbers of marbles are:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Red}&=\\frac{21}{100}\\times10\\\\\\text{Red}&=2.1\\approx2\\\\\\text{Green}&=\\frac{32}{100}\\times10\\\\\\text{Green}&=3.2\\approx3\\\\\\text{Blue}&=\\frac{47}{100}\\times10\\\\\\text{Blue}&=4.7\\approx5\\end{align*}$$\nThese whole-marble estimates total $2+3+5=10$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q13-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "For each of the following, state whether it is a possible set of colours for the 10 marbles.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p28-q13-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "3 red, 3 green, 4 blue",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Yes.",
              "worked": "$3+3+4=10$, and every observed colour is present. Experimental relative frequencies can differ from the proportions in the bag.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 8
          },
          {
            "id": "p28-q13-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "2 red, 4 green, 4 blue",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Yes.",
              "worked": "$2+4+4=10$, and every observed colour is present. Variation in the experimental results is possible.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 8
          },
          {
            "id": "p28-q13-b-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "2 red, 3 green, 4 blue, 1 purple",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Yes.",
              "worked": "$2+3+4+1=10$, and every observed colour is present. A purple marble could remain unselected in the 100 trials.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 8
          },
          {
            "id": "p28-q13-b-iv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "2 red, 0 green, 8 blue",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
